#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# khinchin

#% text
# `khinchin` is Khinchin's constant 2.6854..., the limit of the geometric mean of the continued fraction terms of almost every real number.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `n(khinchin, p)` sums the series `ln K = (1/ln 2) sum over k of (zeta(2k) - 1)/k (1 - 1/2 + ... - 1/(2k - 1))`, whose terms fall like `4^-k`.

#% item
# It is a symbol that `n` turns into numbers; it is not used inside larger expressions by `n` yet.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
n(khinchin)
#% output
#= 2.6854520010653062

#% cell
n(khinchin, 30)
#% output
#= 2.685452001065306445309714835481796

#% cell
n(khinchin, 50)
#% output
#= 2.685452001065306445309714835481795693820382293994462953

#% cell
n(product(map(t => t^(1/200), continued_fraction(pi, 200))))
#% output
#= 2.727377466661712

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `continued_fraction`, `euler_gamma`
